      'The Depth Question: More layers generally extracts more features - but in medical imaging with limited data, deeper models overfit. The right depth is an empirical question, not a default.',
      'Dropout Trade-off: Dropout is a standard regularisation technique, but applying it aggressively to already-shallow architectures can destroy the features the model needs. Getting the balance right required systematic experimentation.',
      'Dataset Size Constraint: 5,666 images is small by deep learning standards. Every architectural decision - layer count, dropout rate, input size - has outsized impact at this scale.',
