      'This project came from a real place - growing up in a small town in Himachal Pradesh where doctors visited once or twice a week. A close friend\'s fracture went undiagnosed for nearly two weeks. X-AI Care is a direct response to that gap. It\'s a prototype, not a deployed product - but it demonstrates what responsible, explainable medical AI looks like when built with the right priorities: transparency first, never replacing the doctor, always showing its work.',
    impactDetails: [
      'Personal Motivation: Built to solve a problem I witnessed firsthand - rural healthcare access gaps where diagnostic delays cause preventable harm.',
      'Explainability Over Accuracy: Most medical AI demos chase benchmark numbers. This one prioritises showing why the model made a decision, which is what clinical trust actually requires.',
      'Two Audiences, One System: The dual report design recognises that a doctor and a patient need different things from the same information - technical rigour for one, empathy and clarity for the other.',
      'Honest About Limitations: Confidence scoring and explicit disclaimers mean the system actively resists overreach. It tells users when it\'s uncertain and when to see a real doctor.',
      'Extensible Foundation: The modular pipeline means new conditions can be added without architectural changes - the system is designed to grow.',
    ],
    limitations: [
      'Prototype Stage: Trained on limited datasets for wrist and cataract detection. Requires extensive clinical validation before real-world use.',
      'Model Diversity: Currently covers two conditions. Expanding requires new labelled datasets and retraining.',
      'Computational Overhead: Grad-CAM and SHAP add latency. Not suitable for real-time or resource-constrained edge deployment in current form.',
      'Dataset Bias: Prototype models trained on limited demographic data. Fairness audits needed before any clinical deployment.',
      'Regulatory Path: Medical AI requires regulatory approval and compliance. This is a research prototype, not a certified clinical tool.',
    ],
    technologies: ['Python', 'TensorFlow', 'PyTorch', 'Grad-CAM', 'SHAP', 'GPT OSS', 'Flask', 'React', 'PostgreSQL', 'OpenCV', 'Scikit-learn', 'HuggingFace Transformers'],
